/pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="other">Morton DL, Cochran AJ, Thompson JF: Authors&#x02019; reply to a letter to the editor re: Sentinel-Node Biopsy in Melanoma. N Engl J Med 356:418&#x02013;9;author reply 419&#x02013;21, 2007</citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pawlik</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ross</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Predictors and natural history of in-transit melanoma after sentinel lymphadenectomy</article-title><source>Ann Surg Oncol</source><year>2005</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>587</fpage><lpage>96</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1245/ASO.2005.05.025</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Pawlik TM, Ross MI, Johnson MM, et al: Predictors and natural history of in-transit melanoma after sentinel lymphadenectomy. Ann Surg Oncol 12:587&#x02013;96, 2005 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16021533</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pawlik</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ross</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The risk of in-transit melanoma metastasis depends on tumor biology and not the surgical approach to regional lymph nodes</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>2005</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>4588</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1200/JCO.2005.12.245</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Pawlik TM, Ross MI, Thompson JF, et al: The risk of in-transit melanoma metastasis depends on tumor biology and not the surgical approach to regional lymph nodes. J Clin Oncol 23:4588&#x02013;90, 2005 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16034040</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kang</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wanek</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Essner</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Sentinel lymphadenectomy does not increase the incidence of in-transit metastases in primary melanoma</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>2005</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>4764</fpage><lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1200/JCO.2005.20.537</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kang JC, Wanek LA, Essner R, et al: Sentinel lymphadenectomy does not increase the incidence of in-transit metastases in primary melanoma. J Clin Oncol 23:4764&#x02013;70, 2005 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16034052</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Poll</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Colman</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A sentinel node biopsy does not increase the incidence of in-transit metastasis in patients with primary cutaneous melanoma</article-title><source>Ann Surg Oncol</source><year>2005</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>597</fpage><lpage>608</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1245/ASO.2005.08.012</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">van Poll D, Thompson JF, Colman MH, et al: A sentinel node biopsy does not increase the incidence of in-transit metastasis in patients with primary cutaneous melanoma. Ann Surg Oncol 12:597&#x02013;608, 2005 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16021534</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wrightson</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Complications associated with sentinel lymph node biopsy for melanoma</article-title><source>Ann Surg Oncol</source><year>2003</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>676</fpage><lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1245/ASO.2003.10.001</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Wrightson WR, Wong SL, Edwards MJ, et al: Complications associated with sentinel lymph node biopsy for melanoma. Ann Surg Oncol 10:676&#x02013;80, 2003 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12839853</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>